size    v d (v)TG (v)/M [5, Theorem 1]; the size is independent of the chosen cyclic orders.
The Eulerian tour case is also treated in Holroyd et al. [2, Theorem 3.8]. These are not our
contribution. A barbell with cycle lengths 3, 3 and bridge length 1 has pointer period 16 below,
whereas its bidirected Eulerian rotor graph has 14 arcs and recurrent period 14. This excludes
only a time-preserving identification on that same core, not factors, suspensions, enlarged states
or arbitrary rotor encodings.
